  Relationships (as drawn):
    Dim_Customer (1) ---- "who bought" ---- (N) Fact_Sales
    Dim_Product  (1) ---- "what was sold" -- (N) Fact_Sales
    Fact_Sales   (N) ---- "when" ---------- (1) Dim_Date
Snowflake schema
A snowflake schema is the normalized form of the star schema. The dimension tables are split into
sub-dimension tables (normalized up to 3NF) using foreign keys: Customer to City, Product to
Category. The diagram looks like a snowflake.

